Algorithm: MATLAB Ground Station Telemetry Reception and CCSDS Decoding

1.	Configure serial communication. 
2.	Continuously monitor the serial port for the start-of-frame marker. 
3.	Read the received frame length. 
4.	Read the complete CCSDS frame. 
5.	Read the receiver-measured RSSI and SNR values. 
6.	Verify the end-of-frame marker. 
7.	Verify the minimum frame length. 
8.	Extract and decode the CCSDS-inspired primary header:
a.	Version
b.	Packet Type
c.	Secondary Header Flag
d.	APID
e.	Sequence Counter
f.	Payload Length
9.	Verify complete frame reception. 
10.	Compute the CCSDS CRC-16. 
11.	Compare the computed CRC with the received CRC. 
12.	If CRC verification fails, 
    -	discard the packet. 
14.	Otherwise, 
    -	extract the payload from the CCSDS frame. 
15.	Decode the telemetry fields using regular expression matching. 
16.	Convert the extracted telemetry strings into numerical values. 
17.	Display the decoded telemetry together with the measured RSSI and SNR. 
18.	Repeat.